1
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,780
This is Trigun.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,380
Oh, my God.

3
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:42,580
Meryl, look!

4
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:50,130
Meryl?

5
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:52,030
Meryl?

6
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:53,780
Meryl, wake up!

7
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:56,197
Oh, um...

8
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:58,320
Oh, hi, Karen.

9
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:00,130
Interesting.

10
00:02:00,213 --> 00:02:01,043
I'm sorry.

11
00:02:01,126 --> 00:02:01,956
I'm sorry.

12
00:02:02,039 --> 00:02:02,869
Did you enjoy your rest?

13
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,597
I've been traveling around for so long,

14
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:08,037
I guess I haven't quite
regained my land legs yet.

15
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:09,885
It must be strange to be home.

16
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:14,477
After all, Miss Strife, you witnessed the
hole being burned into the fifth moon.

17
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:16,497
How did it make you
feel when you looked up?

18
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:18,317
This is not some tourist interview, Mark.

19
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,230
Stop it.

20
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:22,037
You're talking to someone who
spent five months on the outside,

21
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:26,317
working with the ultra-dangerous man
who's been labeled a human disaster.

22
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:28,297
Considering everything that's
happened to her out there,

23
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:30,337
It's a miracle that she came back alive.

24
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:31,537
Yes, but...

25
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:34,200
Actually, it wasn't as bad as all that.

26
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:36,377
Sure, it got a little bit scary at times?

27
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:38,277
And there was some danger involved?

28
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,197
but you know what?

29
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:41,617
Despite his frightening
and awful reputation,

30
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:43,377
Vash turned out to be
more of a regular guy?

31
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:44,357
than you would have thought.

32
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:45,675
Reality check, Meryl.

33
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:49,697
The attitude of yours gets all the oddball
jobs, working with dangerous slime.

34
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:51,837
It's great that you're
so competent and willing,

35
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:53,877
but if you keep risking
your life out there...

36
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:56,357
I'm afraid there's no way you'll
ever achieve womanly happiness.

37
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:57,420
Excuse me.

38
00:02:57,580 --> 00:03:00,051
Is this social time, ladies and gentlemen?

39
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:03,270
Good morning.

40
00:03:03,460 --> 00:03:05,107
It's nice to see you, Chief.

41
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:07,769
Meryl, will you please
step into my office?

42
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:08,690
Sir?

43
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:11,020
I have to what?

44
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:17,460
Millie? Millie? Where
are you? I'm out here.

45
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:18,756
Good morning, Meryl.

46
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:22,254
What have you gotten yourself into now?

47
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:25,937
Well, I'm being punished for coming
in late for work 20 times in a row.

48
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:27,757
Why do I expect her to change?

49
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:28,670
I'm dreaming.

50
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:29,710
Guess what?

51
00:03:29,793 --> 00:03:31,497
We got another assignment today.

52
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:35,117
Vash the Stampede showed up in Little
Jersey, and we're the only ones qualified.

53
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:36,740
We leave right away. Yay!

54
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:37,777
Then it's really true.

55
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:38,857
Vash is still alive.

56
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:41,234
Doesn't that make you incredibly happy?

57
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:44,937
There's nothing to be happy about.

58
00:03:45,020 --> 00:03:46,557
Our jobs are on the line here, Millie.

59
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:50,257
We have to stop him this time
before he stirs up trouble again.

60
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:51,170
Now, come on.

61
00:03:51,253 --> 00:03:52,083
You're wasting time.

62
00:03:52,166 --> 00:03:52,996
Let's get going.

63
00:03:53,079 --> 00:03:54,485
Wait, hold on a second, Meryl.

64
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:55,937
Aren't you being a little hasty?

65
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:59,457
For crying out loud, if he's alive,
he could have at least mentioned it.

66
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:03,011
He probably gets a kick out of
making people bite his dust.

67
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:04,040
That bum.

68
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:05,710
Merrill!

69
00:04:05,793 --> 00:04:08,367
I'll bring you back an
AAP bag as a souvenir.

70
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:09,735
See you later, Karen!

71
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,360
Oh, well. It's no use.

72
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:17,715
There she goes again.

73
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:21,846
I suppose there's just some girls
who need to risk their lives.

74
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,337
If you're dead, you don't
have to say anything,

75
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:34,317
but if you're alive, I would appreciate
if you fellas would say something.

76
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:35,640
I'll give you a lift.

77
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:38,120
Uh, gee.

78
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:39,673
Gee, bless you, mister.

79
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:45,500
Yeah, I am pretty damn happy to be alive.

80
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:52,340
Why is it that I always run into
so much trouble when you're around?

81
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:56,257
You're not a very
methodical person, are you?

82
00:04:56,340 --> 00:04:59,257
Normally when you buy a used bike,
you're supposed to repair it, you know,

83
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:03,077
make sure it's in decent condition before
you decide to take it out and ride it.

84
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:06,260
Are you dissing my beautiful
shiny Angelina Tuvas?

85
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,997
Actually, I'm dissing you, not
your stupid broken motorcycle!

86
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:11,700
Come again, needle noggin?

87
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:13,737
Hey, who you calling needle noggin?

88
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:15,644
I say it's pretty darn obvious!

89
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:22,777
Now look what you've done, you idiot!

90
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:24,625
Oh, so now it's my fault, huh?

91
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:26,957
Shut up back there, or
I'll have to fool you out!

92
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,480
Well, is that me?

93
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:30,286
Yes, sir, we're really sorry.

94
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:32,837
All right, now where are you guys headed?

95
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:33,750
Kansas.

96
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:34,663
New Oregon.

97
00:05:34,746 --> 00:05:35,576
Huh?

98
00:05:35,659 --> 00:05:36,740
Uh, New Oregon?

99
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:40,177
We're going to the town with all the
disappearances in Southern Cornelia.

100
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:41,737
No, I want to go to New Oregon.

101
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:44,317
If you want to go to Kansas,
go there by yourself!

102
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,577
You're going to, sir!

103
00:05:45,660 --> 00:05:47,248
I said, shut up, your turn!

104
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:49,020
Huh? We're sorry.

105
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:54,980
This place is really falling apart

106
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:58,817
Go over where we're from making
trouble as usual Then all of

107
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:01,677
a sudden this guy stepped in to
help Seemed like a pretty well

108
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:04,677
-meaning fella And unfortunately
this is what happened as a

109
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:08,417
result Once again he's poked his
nose into more trouble Honestly,

110
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:10,300
that man never learns Meryl!

111
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:13,876
I just found out where Vash
is and they said he's okay

112
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:15,150
Vash?

113
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:16,390
Yep,

114
00:06:16,473 --> 00:06:18,777
the one and only humanoid
typhoon He carries the dubious

115
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:21,757
title of mankind's first
localized human disaster.

116
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:22,899
That's ridiculous.

117
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:23,837
When I saw him,

118
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:28,332
he was weeping and eating piles of
donuts at the same time, just like this.

119
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,377
Donuts are his favorite food.

120
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:31,480
It's really him?

121
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:32,677
I can't believe it.

122
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:34,977
This nutcase is actually
the legendary gunman?

123
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:37,117
So where'd you get your
information, Millie?

124
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:38,077
Over the satellite.

125
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:39,357
Everyone's talking about it.

126
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:42,997
The report said that he's headed for New
Oregon at a speed of 3,000 yards an hour.

127
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:43,910
Isn't that incredible?

128
00:06:43,993 --> 00:06:45,157
He can move really fast.

129
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:47,557
That's a little more
information than I needed.

130
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:48,470
Yeah, I know.

131
00:06:48,553 --> 00:06:52,749
And one of the locals was even running
around telling everyone to be careful.

132
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:54,480
You can't be serious.

133
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:56,977
The day before yesterday,

134
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,137
most of the Polo family went out of town,

135
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:02,044
leaving no one there but
the fourth son, Slater.

136
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:05,617
Also, I found there's a shuttle
that goes to New Oregon.

137
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:06,530
It's ideal.

138
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:09,657
A chance like this
doesn't come twice. I...

139
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:11,017
I don't know about this.

140
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:12,394
All right, I'll do it.

141
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:16,297
I think we all agree the Polo family can't
be allowed to have their way anymore.

142
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:17,210
Huh?

143
00:07:17,293 --> 00:07:18,123
Aren't I right?

144
00:07:18,206 --> 00:07:19,036
Right.

145
00:07:19,119 --> 00:07:19,949
Well, sort of.

146
00:07:20,032 --> 00:07:21,037
At least this time, we'll have Mr.

147
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,637
Rinald with us to back us up.

148
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:23,779
Yeah, that's true.

149
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:25,897
That settles it, then.

150
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:27,597
All right, gentlemen, this is it.

151
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:30,033
We'll meet here again at sunup tomorrow.

152
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,880
Shut up and listen up!

153
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:37,297
Today I'm going to school you people!

154
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:39,480
Today's lesson is about typhoons!

155
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:41,637
Since you probably don't know, here I go!

156
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:45,017
A typhoon is a little phenomenon
where the wind blows like

157
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:48,394
crazy and carries your houses
and tins off into the sky.

158
00:07:48,660 --> 00:07:53,200
Her name is Jacqueline, and this lovely
young lady has come to wipe you out.

159
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,957
What's all this about, Mr.

160
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:55,870
Typhoon?

161
00:07:55,953 --> 00:07:58,297
Are you expecting a relative
of yours sometime soon?

162
00:07:58,380 --> 00:08:00,145
So, is that what a typhoon is?

163
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:04,124
A furious beauty who levels entire
cities without even a warning.

164
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:05,310
A beauty?

165
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:07,900
Sounds pretty tough.

166
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:11,817
Hey, by the way, who's picking
up the tab for this little food?

167
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:12,940
Me? Why me?

168
00:08:13,180 --> 00:08:15,277
I was the one gracious enough
to give it to your stupid

169
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:17,517
whining and come all the
way out here to New Oregon.

170
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:19,129
Didn't ask you to do that.

171
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:20,880
Now listen up.

172
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:22,377
This town may look peaceful,

173
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:25,617
but things are likely to get
bloody around here at any time.

174
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:27,137
I don't know if you're aware of this,

175
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:29,297
but the Polo and Frieze
families are still quarreling!

176
00:08:29,380 --> 00:08:30,897
over their rights to the satellite.

177
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:34,677
A girl who was a distant cousin of the
Frieze family was murdered in cold blood.

178
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:36,172
It's a high-stakes feud.

179
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:39,477
The more I think about it,

180
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:42,177
but I don't want this town to
turn into another little jersey.

181
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:44,436
Let's take off before it's destroyed.

182
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:47,260
Knock it off!

183
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:49,776
But doesn't that story get you upset?

184
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:52,234
Why do things like that have to happen?

185
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:53,837
It's not like it's anything new.

186
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:55,597
This kind of thing happens all the time.

187
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,937
Even the most peaceful
folk will take up arms if

188
00:08:58,020 --> 00:09:00,597
someone happens to threaten
or kill a family member.

189
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:04,209
Bottom line is, we should go
before we get involved in this.

190
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:07,357
I've always had my suspicions
that you were no mere mortal,

191
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:10,087
but I never imagined
you were actually a cat.

192
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:12,880
Wait, what the hell am I saying?

193
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:14,760
Where is that idiot? Sir?

194
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:18,577
Altogether, your meal
comes to exactly $30.

195
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:20,460
Put it on my tab? No, thanks.

196
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:23,100
Rotten needle noggin.

197
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:26,940
Uh, Mr.

198
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:30,354
Slater, there's a hick outside
asking to be let in, sir.

199
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:31,410
Sir?

200
00:09:31,493 --> 00:09:34,242
I'm not interested in any
beggars or job hunters.

201
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:35,856
Just send them away.

202
00:09:35,980 --> 00:09:38,497
A friend of mine works here,
and I was in the neighborhood.

203
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:40,497
I just thought I'd drop
by to say hi to him.

204
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:43,277
Hey, I didn't say you could
come in here, street worm.

205
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:44,772
Who are you here to see?

206
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:46,380
His name is Max Simon.

207
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:48,816
That old codger actually has friends?

208
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,637
Go ahead, entertain him.

209
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:51,957
All right, thanks a lot.

210
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:53,520
I appreciate it. Bye.

211
00:09:54,860 --> 00:09:56,154
Sure about this, boss?

212
00:09:56,380 --> 00:09:57,909
Do I really have a choice?

213
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:02,141
He's a friend of Max's, and I'm
not about to start any trouble now.

214
00:10:04,220 --> 00:10:05,520
This was a good idea.

215
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:08,897
We did the right thing to splurge
on a room in second class.

216
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:12,057
Yeah, the last time we were when
it is, it was full advantage.

217
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:13,997
The whole experience was ruined.

218
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:16,877
If we run into him in New Oregon,
things are gonna get real busy.

219
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:19,136
Let's enjoy the peace while it lasts.

220
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:23,358
I guess that means we're going to
get dragged into trouble again, huh?

221
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:27,180
Oh, my thunder!

222
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:29,857
Hands with the air and mouth shut.

223
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:31,377
He's better not trying anything funny.

224
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:32,520
You understand me?

225
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:35,480
Not an end!

226
00:10:49,340 --> 00:10:52,680
I suggest you all behave
if you value your lives.

227
00:10:55,020 --> 00:10:57,437
Make this easy on yourself and don't move.

228
00:10:57,520 --> 00:11:00,477
I promise you won't be
harmed if you just cooperate.

229
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:03,637
You have a chance to stop this right
now and the law will be more lenient.

230
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:06,680
I gave up my life a
long time ago. Besides,

231
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:11,469
there's a damn good reason I'm doing
this, and I don't care what the cost is.

232
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:14,317
We've almost reached our destination.

233
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,977
Make sure you keep an eye on him.

234
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:16,890
Got it.

235
00:11:16,973 --> 00:11:20,153
If she were alive, she'd be
about your age now, you know?

236
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:26,857
I'm not finished with the forecast.

237
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:28,317
Beat it, leave me alone.

238
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:31,047
I can see you haven't
changed a bit, old man.

239
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:32,150
Vash!

240
00:11:32,820 --> 00:11:34,408
It's been a very long time.

241
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:36,717
What happened to the old snappy outfit?

242
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:39,388
I guess I kind of wore
it out on my last job

243
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:41,190
Well,

244
00:11:41,273 --> 00:11:44,857
welcome back you are here on business or
just come to pick up Jacqueline's dress

245
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:45,770
Hmm.

246
00:11:45,853 --> 00:11:49,034
Has it really been ten years
since your last visit Vash?

247
00:12:02,020 --> 00:12:03,200
No, Marcy!

248
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:04,860
Kill anyone every day!

249
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:08,120
Where is he?

250
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:09,640
I want him!

251
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:12,320
Holy cow!

252
00:12:12,580 --> 00:12:16,840
A Monsterian just crashed a sand
steamer into my exalted place of work!

253
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:21,317
I've heard of people falling asleep
at the wheel, but this is ridiculous!

254
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:22,400
Mr. F!

255
00:12:32,340 --> 00:12:33,557
Pardon me, coming through.

256
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:34,470
Excuse me, lady.

257
